Subject: engine: a refused AOT unit says why, once

What this does
  aot_unit_present reports the reason before it returns zero: one line on stderr
  naming the cause and both hashes, for an ABI mismatch or a layout mismatch.
  The flag that guards it keeps it to one line per process.

Why we need it
  A unit that is linked but refused is not an error the program can see. The
  engine falls back to the interpreter, which is correct and several times
  slower, with no diagnostic anywhere, so the only symptom of a misbuilt binary
  is a program that runs at the wrong speed. The condition is always a mismatch
  between the layout the unit was generated against and the engine's own, and
  the two hashes are the whole diagnosis.

Hazards
  The message goes to stderr at the first binding attempt, which is the first
  compiled call, not at init: a run that never reaches a compiled function never
  prints it. Nothing else changes -- the return value, the binding table and the
  fallback path are as they were.

Tests: a refusal is forced by linking a unit whose layout hash is wrong and the
line is checked, once per process; the kit outputs for richards, deltablue, nbody
and raytrace are unchanged, and no line is printed when the unit binds.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -63597,12 +63597,34 @@
     return l.hash;
 }
 
+/* A unit that is linked but refused runs the program in the interpreter
+   with no other sign; one line on stderr, once per process, names
+   the cause and both hashes. */
+static int aot_unit_refused_reported;
+
 static int aot_unit_present(void)
 {
 #if defined(__GNUC__)
-    return (&qjs_aot_count != NULL) && (&qjs_aot_layout != NULL) &&
-           qjs_aot_abi == QJS_AOT_ABI &&
-           qjs_aot_layout == js_aot_unit_layout_hash();
+    int has_unit = (&qjs_aot_count != NULL) && (&qjs_aot_layout != NULL);
+
+    if (!has_unit)
+        return 0;
+    if (qjs_aot_abi == QJS_AOT_ABI && qjs_aot_layout == js_aot_unit_layout_hash())
+        return 1;
+    if (!aot_unit_refused_reported) {
+        aot_unit_refused_reported = 1;
+        if (qjs_aot_abi != QJS_AOT_ABI)
+            fprintf(stderr,
+                    "quickjs: AOT unit refused: ABI mismatch (unit %u, engine %u)\n",
+                    (unsigned)qjs_aot_abi, (unsigned)QJS_AOT_ABI);
+        else
+            fprintf(stderr,
+                    "quickjs: AOT unit refused: engine layout mismatch "
+                    "(unit %u, engine %u)\n",
+                    (unsigned)qjs_aot_layout,
+                    (unsigned)js_aot_unit_layout_hash());
+    }
+    return 0;
 #else
     return 0;
 #endif
